    "This file is the data SpikeScore starts with. Edit it, save, then fully restart the app (stop it and run again).",
    "match: the details printed in the header of the scoresheet. Delete a line to leave that box blank.",
    "match.home / match.away: the 'id' of the two teams that are playing. Change these to swap teams.",
    "match.date is YYYY-MM-DD and match.time is HH:MM (24 hour). match.category is men, women or mixed.",
    "teams: the library of teams. Add as many as you like, copying one of the blocks below.",
    "players: shirt number, name and position. Shirt numbers must be different within a team. The sheet has room for 13 players. A player with position Libero is also listed in the libero rows.",
    "startingLineup: the six starters in service order, I to VI (the first number serves first). If it is missing or wrong, the first six non-libero players are used.",
    "officials: role is C (coach), AC (assistant coach), T (trainer) or M (medical). The sheet has room for 4 per team.",
    "If you change a team, the match that was saved on the phone is dropped automatically so it can't clash with the new data.",
    "If this file has a mistake, the app shows an orange message at the top and uses its built-in teams until it is fixed."
